<title>UK: Hopes of averting UK rail strikes rise after deal.</title>
<headline>Hopes of averting UK rail strikes rise after deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hopes that British strikes planned for Friday at several train operators can be averted rose on Thursday when two companies reached deals with the main rail union.</p>
<p>South West Trains, which runs services out of London Waterloo, and Cardiff Railways agreed to cut the hours of train crews from 39 to 37 a week in line with other recent settlements.</p>
<p>Talks are continuing between the Rail Maritime and Transport union and managers at other companies to try to head off Friday's planned walkout.</p>
</text>
